WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.040
There was a bit of a sort of second honeymoon
phase for Donald Trump early in the Corona

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:09.910
virus pandemic, and we talked about it at
the time, his approval rating on his handling

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.579
of the Corona virus pandemic was actually
not bad. Early on, his general presidential

00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:19.010
approval had actually ticked up in mid-March
to close to 50 percent, which is very close

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:23.250
to a high for Donald Trump's presidency. And
this wasn't shocking. And as we talked about

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:28.599
at the time, there is this historical sort
of rally around the president tendency during

00:00:28.599 --> 00:00:34.570
times of national crisis. We saw after 9/11,
for example, George W. Bush's approval spiked

00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:40.710
dramatically to as high as 90 percent, which
is it's almost unthinkable today.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.430
Of course, it was eventually squandered by
George W. Bush, but then it spiked again as

00:00:45.430 --> 00:00:52.079
the Iraq war got going in early 2003, all
the way up to 71 percent approval. And then

00:00:52.079 --> 00:00:56.980
again, that fell off for George W. Bush as
that war ended up being a completely misguided

00:00:56.980 --> 00:01:02.170
disaster. And Donald Trump had a little bit
of this in March, back in March. His approval

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:09.090
ticked up. But as his as his administration's
response to the virus has tragically been

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:12.610
one of the worst in the world. I mean, I'm
not going to say the worst, but you have to

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:19.130
look pretty hard for leaders who responded
more poorly than Donald Trump did. We have

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:25.400
seen Donald Trump experience the sharpest
drop in approval of his presidency so far.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:32.120
Now, the news here for now is the rapid change
so far. OK. The absolute numbers are still

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:38.350
in the normal range for Trump's presidency.
His approvals down to 43. That's not the absolute

00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:44.350
low of his presidency. His disapproval spiked
to 54. Again, that's not the high disapproval

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:49.140
of his presidency. But if you're looking at
the chart with me right now, you see that

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:56.219
this is a very rapid nine point jump in disapproval
since the last time Gallup did the survey.

00:01:56.219 --> 00:02:02.530
And a nine point jump in three weeks is the
biggest, fastest jump in that time period

00:02:02.530 --> 00:02:08.070
during the presidency. Now, where will it
go next? We don't know, but it's clear that

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:15.370
Americans are on average realizing the disaster
that is Donald Trump handling a true crisis.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:21.920
Now, his supporters are still absolutely enamored
with his handling. They now are increasingly

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:26.120
protesting for the reopening of states with
Trump increasingly supporting them. We'll

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:31.830
talk about that a little bit later. But at
the national level, on average, Trump's approval

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:36.410
has declined very quickly over the last three
weeks. Now, in the meantime, the polling for

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:41.580
Joe Biden in the 20 20 presidential election,
which is now just six and a half months away,

00:02:41.580 --> 00:02:47.510
continues to be strong. But I'm going to keep
being very careful about this. All that I'm

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:53.731
telling you today is that right now, six and
a half months before the election, there is

00:02:53.731 --> 00:02:59.460
a trend in which Joe Biden isn't doing poorly
against Donald Trump. The trend is that the

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:05.340
country is, as I said already, it's on average
a country that disapproves of Donald Trump

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:10.100
and is a country that on average is leaning
towards Joe Biden. But things can change quickly.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:14.260
And remember that we have an electoral college
in the United States. So in the latest NBC

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:21.960
News Wall Street Journal poll, Biden is plus
seven over, Trump 49 to 42. That still leaves

00:03:21.960 --> 00:03:28.580
a full 9 percent unsure or with third parties.
Right now, we then have a Harvard Harris poll,

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:35.010
which has Biden plus six. In this one, it's
Biden 53, Trump 47. That one has no undecideds.

00:03:35.010 --> 00:03:40.770
Now, this could mean nothing by November and
Trump may get himself reelected. And so we

00:03:40.770 --> 00:03:46.620
have to be very careful about inferring much
at all from this. Interesting. Also in North

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.690
Carolina, Biden is now plus one in a recent
poll. Trump had actually been winning in North

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:57.810
Carolina in a bunch of recent polls. So that's
a big flip. The caveat being this is a P P

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:05.060
P poll. P P P polls are known for leaning
Democratic. It may mean very little, but if

00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:12.290
Biden can stay close in North Carolina, that's
a state that Trump won by three plus in 2016.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:19.681
If it's even if Biden is really plus one in
North Carolina, that could set suggest a worse

00:04:19.681 --> 00:04:26.130
outcome for Trump in 2020 than he had in 2016.
The important takeaways are we're counting

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:31.940
every vote. We're not opting out. I'm speaking
of optimistically. None of us are opting out

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:36.270
of the election. We're pushing for vote by
mail and the expansion of absentee ballots

00:04:36.270 --> 00:04:42.380
so that we can keep people safe and voting
in November. Nothing changes for us as a result

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:48.210
of these numbers. We want no one to die or
go without corona virus care. You know, Republicans

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:54.790
are now trying to give some oxygen to this
theory that the left wants more people to

00:04:54.790 --> 00:05:00.610
die from the virus so that it will be bad
for Donald Trump. Trump has already failed.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:06.010
No one else needs to die for Trump to deserve
being removed in November. And I think that

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:09.310
that's the important thing that we have to
point out. Every time they say you want a

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:15.260
higher death toll, we say that's absolutely
ridiculous. There's no evidence of that. And

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:21.330
it's not about a higher death toll to justify
Trump's removal. Trump's rhetoric and actions

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:27.930
to date already justify his removal, even
if the deaths went to zero today. It's a false

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:33.780
premise. Don't let them trick you into these
red herrings, but also don't get lulled into

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.090
any sense of complacency because of these
numbers.

